      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Mix the pork mince, glass noodles, mushrooms, carrot, shallots, egg, fish sauce, and sugar in a bowl until combined. Squeeze out any excess liquid from the carrot and mushrooms first."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Dip a sheet of rice paper in warm water for about 5 seconds until barely pliable. Lay flat on a damp surface."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Place 2 tablespoons of filling in a log shape across the lower third of the wrapper. Fold the bottom edge over the filling, then fold in the sides, and roll up tightly."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Repeat with the remaining wrappers and filling. Keep completed rolls on a lightly oiled plate to prevent sticking."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat the oil in a large saucepan to 175°C. Test with a small piece of wrapper . it should sizzle and float immediately."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Fry the rolls in batches of 4 to 5. Cook for 5 to 6 minutes, turning occasionally, until deep golden and crispy. Drain on a wire rack."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Mix the dipping sauce ingredients together with 3 tbsp of water. Serve the rolls immediately with the dipping sauce and fresh herbs."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "The rolls burst open during frying.",
              "cause": "The filling was too wet or the roll was not sealed tightly enough.",
              "fix": "Squeeze all excess moisture from the filling ingredients. Roll tightly and press the seam firmly to seal."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "The wrapper is thick and chewy instead of crispy.",
              "cause": "The oil was not hot enough.",
              "fix": "Maintain the oil at 175°C throughout frying. If the oil is too cool, the wrapper absorbs oil and turns chewy."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "The rice paper tears when wrapping.",
              "cause": "The wrapper was over-soaked.",
              "fix": "Dip the rice paper for only 5 seconds. It should feel stiff and barely pliable. It will soften more as you roll."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Nem rán is the name used in northern Vietnam for fried spring rolls. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "In the south, the same dish is called chả giò. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Fried spring rolls are eaten at family celebrations, festivals, and as everyday street food. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "They are one of the most widely recognised Vietnamese foods outside the country. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Each family has its own filling recipe passed down through generations."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
